# The dot call of Julia (P50, notes/broadcasting.md), the phrase `f .( (x)` of the parser: any function applied to each
# item whatever it takes, by the broadcasting words (prelude each_any, element_wise_any): length.(["ab", "c"]) is
# [2 1], max.(u, v) pairs the items. First sugar: a later pass reads the phrase as a call of its first word; the dot
# asks for the broadcast, so no guard: of a value not known to be a list each_any decides at run time
rewrite $f.($x) => each_any($x, $e -> $f($e))
rewrite $f.($a, $b) => element_wise_any($a, $b, ($l, $r) -> $f($l, $r))
